        "text": "Another popular DEFI application is decentralized exchanges, often called DEXs. These platforms allow users to trade or swap digital assets without a trusted intermediary. The trades are made directly between user wallets with the help of smart contracts. Some exchanges, known as automated market makers, use liquidity pools to facilitate trading without directly needing a counterparty to match your trade. You can think of them as a robot always willing to quote you a price between two assets, essentially allowing anyone to become a market maker on an exchange and earn fees for providing liquidity.",
